rance","to another fragrance,","I used to go.","Now I am very alone.","Before me is a clamour,","yet I am silent, motionless.","Now I cannot recall","the dearest memory.","Passing along the road,","unblinking there appears","a leafless,","fruit-laden tree;","it seems so incongruous.","Within me","are so many incongruous scenes","I cannot show to anyone.","On branch after branch of the tree,","so many letters,","and so many more letters","against the foundation of the sky;","I cannot read a thing.","Who steals away","the enchantment of the letters' conversation,","I cannot know.","Now I am very alone;","the torment of a sleepless night,","the dreams all so very pale."]],"inline_breaks":[],"hidden_lines":[]}},"end_mark":"leaf","author":"Jayanti Rath","route":"poem-36.html","portrait":"assets/writers/71-earth-voice-v2-64.webp","illustration":{"src":"assets/section-art/reader-letters-poetic-natural.webp","alt":"Letters and an earthen teacup rest on a small wooden stool.","width":1536,"height":1024},"availability":""}]}
